# --- large raw competition rasters (byte-verified, re-fetchable) ---
# training_features.tif alone is 419 MB; scripts/fetch_data.sh re-fetches and
# re-hashes all three against the SHA-256 pins in evidence/data_provenance.json.
data/*.tif
data/*.zip
data/raw/
data/features/
!data/README.md

# --- generated caches: 4.4 GB, all reproducible by scripts/03 + scripts/04 ---
# features.f16 is 3.83 GB; the per-fold oof_* maps are 49 MB each. Only the small
# layer-name manifests are kept, because they are the audit trail for which
# features existed and which were excluded as catalogue-derived (leakage control).
data/derived/*
!data/derived/*.json

# --- large DERIVED external layers (91 MB total) -----------------------------
# These are predecessor-session products, not deliverables, and each one is pinned
# by SHA-256 + DOI/ScienceBase id in the sibling .json provenance file that IS
# committed. Re-fetch per scripts/fetch_data.sh. The small external layers that
# the holdout actually depends on (derived_sgmc_faults_100m_u8.tif, the GDR CSVs,
# template-mask.tif, qfaults_prior_u8.tif) are deliberately NOT ignored.
assets/external/lidar_scarp_features_u8.tif
assets/external/geodawn_extensions_u8.tif
assets/external/geodawn_rad_u8.tif

# --- local staging copy of the submission ------------------------------------
# docs/downloads/ is the canonical, served copy (GitHub Pages one-click download)
# and IS committed. submissions/ is a duplicate written by scripts/05;
# scripts/05b_reverify_published.py skips it when absent.
submissions/
# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
